<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Manila Bay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1898</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> Bay was fought on 1 May 1898, at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a>, when the US Asiatic Squadron under Commodore George Dewey destroyed the Spanish Pacific squadron of Admiral Patricio Montojo off Cavite in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. The Americans lost no ships and very few men. The victory led to the American capture of Manila and the end of Spanish rule in the Philippines.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-manila-bay.jpg" alt="Battle of Manila Bay" width="320" height="142" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Gale Tyler (1855–1931) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Manila_Bay_by_James_Gale_Tyler_(1898).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
